{
  "root_cause": "The ArrowRight and ArrowLeft keys call adjustDate with a fixed delta of ±1 day, which does not skip dates disabled by the weekend restriction (disableDayFn). Consequently, navigating from a Friday lands on a Saturday, violating the requirement that weekends are unavailable.",
  "repair_strategy": "Replace the direct adjustDate calls for ArrowLeft (keyCode 37) and ArrowRight (keyCode 39) with a new helper method _shiftDate that increments or decrements by one day repeatedly until it finds a date that is within minDate/maxDate and not disabled by disableWeekends or disableDayFn, with a safety limit to avoid infinite loops.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "pikaday.js",
      "sha256": "a50b66482ec18884a7200882e9b523d9192b224b40b296cdd4080530f114fa75",
      "before": "        self._onKeyChange = function(e)
        {
            e = e || window.event;

            if (self.isVisible()) {

                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 1);
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 1);
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }
            }
        },
",
      "after": "        self._onKeyChange = function(e)
        {
            e = e || window.event;

            if (self.isVisible()) {

                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        self._shiftDate('subtract');
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        self._shiftDate('add');
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }
            }
        },
        self._shiftDate = function(sign)
        {
            var opts = this._o;
            var current = this.getDate() || new Date();
            var dayMs = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
            var safety = 0;
            while (true) {
                var candidate = new Date(current.valueOf() + (sign === 'add' ? dayMs : -dayMs));
                if (opts.minDate && candidate < opts.minDate) {
                    break;
                }
                if (opts.maxDate && candidate > opts.maxDate) {
                    break;
                }
                var disabled = false;
                if (opts.disableWeekends) {
                    var day = candidate.getDay();
                    if (day === 0 || day === 6) disabled = true;
                }
                if (!disabled && opts.disableDayFn && opts.disableDayFn(candidate)) {
                    disabled = true;
                }
                if (!disabled) {
                    this.setDate(candidate);
                    return;
                }
                current = candidate;
                if (++safety > 1000) break;
            }
            // If we exit loop without finding a valid date, do nothing.
        },
"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Keyboard users can now navigate dates with the arrow keys while skipping Saturdays and Sundays, ensuring that only weekdays are reachable. This satisfies WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) and 2.4.3 (Focus Order) by providing a logical, accessible focus movement pattern.",
  "functional_risks": "The helper includes a safety counter to prevent infinite loops; if no valid weekday exists within the min/max range, navigation will stop at the boundary. Week navigation (ArrowUp/ArrowDown) remains unchanged and continues to shift by exactly seven days. Mouse-based date selection is unaffected.",
